# 45. Final acceptance criteria

Do not call the MVP operational until all statements below are true:

```text
Fresh clone builds without undocumented local state.

Fresh database migrates successfully.

Forged auth tokens fail.

Ownership cannot be spoofed.

An ActVersion is immutable and fully hash-bound.

10,000 Submissions can enter a five-slot show.

The deterministic draw is independently replayable.

Only selected Submissions create Appearances.

One audience user cannot manufacture unique crowd size.

EpisodeRoom survives recreation without resetting state.

Stage reconnect receives every missed canonical event.

Human-puppeteered dialogue survives replay.

Prepared minute playback requires no live TTS request.

Episode Zero completes without manual DB edits.

Completed Episode Zero replays without LLM/TTS calls.

No client can fake a payment confirmation.

All above invariants are enforced by CI.
```

Until then, prioritize correctness over feature count.

One especially important correction to the coding agent's new `PROBLEM_REGISTRY`: **API-key SHA-256 is not the security problem worth focusing on**. These keys are generated from high-entropy random bytes, so offline rainbow-table attacks are not analogous to password hashing. The serious issues are that scope checking currently always returns `True`, rate limiting is broken/process-local, and privileged HTTP/WebSocket authorization isn't enforced consistently.

Likewise, the registry says ActVersion hashing is resolved, but the latest `comedians.py` still uses `hexdigest()[:16]` and constructs records using the previous ActVersion schema.  It says the `Submission → Appearance` split is resolved, yet the current episode entry endpoint still creates `Appearance` directly.  Those are good examples of why the project now needs **tests as executable truth**, not more prose saying something is fixed.

I could inspect the repository through the connected GitHub source, but couldn't independently execute a clean checkout in the shell because outbound GitHub DNS is unavailable in this runtime. So I would not treat the commit's “18/18 + 9/11” report as independently verified; more importantly, even if those numbers are accurate, the existing tests do not exercise the critical paths above.
